<title>AUSTRALIA: CRICKET-SHEFFIELD SHIELD RESULTS.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-SHEFFIELD SHIELD RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results on the fourth and final day of first-class Sheffield Shield matches played on Monday:</p>
<p>In Adelaide: South Australia beat Victoria by 161 runs</p>
<p>Scores - South Australia 216 and 449 for nine declared (Darren Lehmann 167, Brad Young 76 not out); Victoria 241 (Ian Harvey 73) and 263.</p>
<p>In Hobart: Tasmania drew with Queensland</p>
<p>Scores - Tasmania 408 (Ricky Ponting 159) and 263 for nine declared (Jamie Cox 74, Michael DiVenuto 56); Queensland 283 (Geoff Foley 77, Matthew Mott 74) and 198 for four (Stuart Law 74 not out)</p>
